inference_trace:
Count how many times each letter appears, then check that every non-zero count is the same.

1. Use an array of 26 counters and increment `cnt[c - 'a']` for each character in `s`.
2. Walk through the counts and skip the zeros, since those letters don't appear.
3. Record the first non-zero count. If any later non-zero count differs from it, return `false`.
4. If the loop finishes without a mismatch, return `true`.

This runs in O(n) time with O(1) extra space.

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean areOccurrencesEqual(String s) {
        int[] cnt = new int[26];
        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) cnt[c - 'a']++;
        int f = 0;
        for (int x : cnt) {
            if (x == 0) continue;
            if (f == 0) f = x;
            else if (x != f) return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

