inference_trace:
Use the cross product. Take the first two points as a reference direction (dx, dy). Every other point (x, y) is on the same line exactly when

dx * (y - y0) == dy * (x - x0).

This avoids division, so vertical lines need no special case.

Each difference is at most 2·10^4 in size, so each product is at most 4·10^8. That fits in an `int`, but `long` is used for safety.

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean checkStraightLine(int[][] coordinates) {
