inference_trace:
Track, for each vowel, how many valid strings of the current length end with that vowel. Start with length 1, where each count is 1.

To extend a string by one character, look at which vowels may come before each ending:

- `a` can follow `e`, `i`, or `u`.
- `e` can follow `a` or `i`.
- `i` can follow `e` or `o`.
- `o` can follow only `i`.
- `u` can follow `i` or `o`.

Repeat this update `n - 1` times, taking every sum modulo `10^9 + 7`. The answer is the sum of the five counts.

This runs in O(n) time and uses O(1) extra space.

```java
class Solution {
    public int countVowelPermutation(int n) {
        final long M = 1_000_000_007L;
        long a = 1, e = 1, i = 1, o = 1, u = 1;
        for (int k = 1; k < n; k++) {
            long na = (e + i + u) % M;
            long ne = (a + i) % M;
            long ni = (e + o) % M;
            long no = i;
            long nu = (i + o) % M;
            a = na; e = ne; i = ni; o = no; u = nu;
        }
        return (int) ((a + e + i + o + u) % M);
    }
}
```

