inference_trace:
Binary search on the answer T. Running all n computers for T minutes is feasible exactly when the total usable charge is enough: sum over batteries of min(b, T) ≥ n·T. A single battery can contribute at most T minutes, because it can only power one computer at a time.

Bounds:
- The answer is at most sum / n.
- sum ≤ 1e14, so it fits in a long.
- min(b, T) summed over 1e5 batteries is at most ~1e14, and n·T ≤ 1e5 · 1e14 = 1e19. That overflows a long, so cap hi at sum / n.
- Since T ≤ sum / n, n·T ≤ sum ≤ 1e14, which is safe.

```java
class Solution {
    public long maxRunTime(int n, int[] batteries) {
        long sum = 0;
        for (int b : batteries) sum += b;
        long lo = 0, hi = sum / n;
        while (lo < hi) {
            long mid = lo + (hi - lo + 1) / 2;
            long total = 0;
            for (int b : batteries) total += Math.min((long) b, mid);
            if (total >= (long) n * mid) lo = mid;
            else hi = mid - 1;
        }
        return lo;
    }
}
```

