Approach: for each non-initial node, find which initial nodes can reach it without passing through any other initial node.

1. Mark every node in `initial` as infected.
2. For each initial node `u`, run a DFS that starts at `u` and walks only through non-infected nodes. Record `u` as an infector of every node it reaches.
3. A non-infected node with exactly one infector `u` is saved if `u` is removed. A node with two or more infectors stays infected no matter which single node is removed.
4. Count saved nodes per initial node. Return the one with the highest count, breaking ties by smallest index.

Removing `u` saves only `u` itself plus the nodes that `u` alone reaches. Since `u` is always saved, comparing the counts of uniquely reached nodes is enough.

Complexity: each DFS costs O(n²) on the adjacency matrix, so the total is O(k·n²), which is fine for n ≤ 300.

```java
class Solution {
    public int minMalwareSpread(int[][] graph, int[] initial) {
        int n = graph.length;
        boolean[] inf = new boolean[n];
        for (int x : initial) inf[x] = true;
        int[] cnt = new int[n];
        int[] who = new int[n];
        java.util.Arrays.fill(who, -1);
        for (int u : initial) {
            boolean[] seen = new boolean[n];
            java.util.ArrayDeque<Integer> st = new java.util.ArrayDeque<>();
            st.push(u);
            seen[u] = true;
            while (!st.isEmpty()) {
                int v = st.pop();
                for (int w = 0; w < n; w++) {
                    if (graph[v][w] == 1 && !seen[w] && !inf[w]) {
                        seen[w] = true;
                        st.push(w);
                        cnt[w]++;
                        who[w] = u;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        int[] save = new int[n];
        for (int v = 0; v < n; v++) {
            if (!inf[v] && cnt[v] == 1) save[who[v]]++;
        }
        int best = -1;
        for (int u : initial) {
            if (best == -1 || save[u] > save[best] || (save[u] == save[best] && u < best)) best = u;
        }
        return best;
    }
}
```

