Count how many positions differ from the pattern `"0101..."`. Call this `cnt`.

Every position that matches `"0101..."` differs from the other pattern `"1010..."`, and vice versa. So the number of changes needed for `"1010..."` is `n - cnt`.

The answer is `min(cnt, n - cnt)`.

To be safe with the trailing spaces shown in the examples, only `'0'` and `'1'` characters are counted toward `n` and the mismatch count; any other character is skipped.

