inference_trace:
Sort the array, then take elements from largest to smallest. Stop as soon as the running sum is strictly greater than the remaining total.

- Taking the largest elements first reaches the threshold with the fewest elements, so the size is minimal.
- For that size, the largest elements also give the maximum total sum.
- Because elements are added largest first, the result is already in non-increasing order.

```java
import java.util.*;

class Solution {
    public List<Integer> minSubsequence(int[] nums) {
        Arrays.sort(nums);
        int total = 0;
        for (int x : nums) total += x;
        List<Integer> res = new ArrayList<>();
        int sum = 0;
        for (int i = nums.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            sum += nums[i];
            res.add(nums[i]);
            if (sum > total - sum) break;
        }
        return res;
    }
}
```

