inference_trace:
Split each cell into 4 triangles and join them with union-find; the answer is the number of connected components.

**Triangle numbering inside a cell:**
- 0 = top
- 1 = right
- 2 = bottom
- 3 = left

**Unions inside a cell:**
- `' '` (blank): union all four triangles.
- `'/'`: union top with left (0–3) and right with bottom (1–2).
- `'\'`: union top with right (0–1) and bottom with left (2–3).

**Unions between neighboring cells:**
- The bottom triangle (2) of cell (i, j) joins the top triangle (0) of cell (i+1, j).
- The right triangle (1) of cell (i, j) joins the left triangle (3) of cell (i, j+1).

The answer starts at 4·n² and drops by one for every union that merges two different sets.

```java
class Solution {
    int[] p;
    int count;
    int find(int x) {
        while (p[x] != x) { p[x] = p[p[x]]; x = p[x]; }
        return x;
    }
    void union(int a, int b) {
        int ra = find(a), rb = find(b);
        if (ra != rb) { p[ra] = rb; count--; }
    }
    public int regionsBySlashes(String[] grid) {
        int n = grid.length;
        p = new int[4 * n * n];
        for (int i = 0; i < p.length; i++) p[i] = i;
        count = 4 * n * n;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                int b = 4 * (i * n + j);
                char c = grid[i].charAt(j);
                if (c == '/') {
                    union(b, b + 3);
                    union(b + 1, b + 2);
                } else if (c == '\\') {
                    union(b, b + 1);
                    union(b + 2, b + 3);
                } else {
                    union(b, b + 1);
                    union(b + 1, b + 2);
                    union(b + 2, b + 3);
                }
                if (i + 1 < n) union(b + 2, 4 * ((i + 1) * n + j));
                if (j + 1 < n) union(b + 1, 4 * (i * n + j + 1) + 3);
            }
        }
        return count;
    }
}
```

