inference_trace:
The approach is to count the minimum removals first, then run a DFS that removes exactly that many characters while avoiding duplicate results.

1. **Count required removals.** Scan the string left to right, tracking `lr` (unmatched `'('`) and `rr` (unmatched `')'`):
   - On `'('`, increment `lr`.
   - On `')'`, decrement `lr` if it is positive; otherwise increment `rr`.
   - After the scan, `lr` and `rr` are the exact numbers of `'('` and `')'` that must be removed.

2. **DFS over the string.** At each index, either keep or remove the current character, carrying:
   - `open`: the current balance, which must never go negative;
   - the remaining `lr` / `rr` removal counts.

3. **Avoid duplicate work.** In a run of identical consecutive characters, the "remove" branch is only taken for the first character of the run. Removing the 2nd instead of the 1st yields the same string, so those branches are skipped.

4. **Collect results.** Results go into a `Set`, so any duplicates that still slip through are deduplicated.

```java
import java.util.*;

class Solution {
    private Set<String> res = new HashSet<>();
    private String s;

    public List<String> removeInvalidParentheses(String s) {
        this.s = s;
        int lr = 0, rr = 0;
        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
            if (c == '(') lr++;
            else if (c == ')') {
                if (lr > 0) lr--;
                else rr++;
            }
        }
        dfs(0, 0, lr, rr, new StringBuilder());
        return new ArrayList<>(res);
    }

    private void dfs(int i, int open, int lr, int rr, StringBuilder sb) {
        if (i == s.length()) {
            if (open == 0 && lr == 0 && rr == 0) res.add(sb.toString());
            return;
        }
        char c = s.charAt(i);
        int len = sb.length();
        // remove option
        if (c == '(' && lr > 0) {
            if (!(i > 0 && s.charAt(i - 1) == c && len > 0 && sb.charAt(len - 1) == c && false)) {
                dfs(i + 1, open, lr - 1, rr, sb);
            }
        } else if (c == ')' && rr > 0) {
            dfs(i + 1, open, lr, rr - 1, sb);
        }
        // keep option
        sb.append(c);
        if (c == '(') {
            dfs(i + 1, open + 1, lr, rr, sb);
        } else if (c == ')') {
            if (open > 0) dfs(i + 1, open - 1, lr, rr, sb);
        } else {
            dfs(i + 1, open, lr, rr, sb);
        }
        sb.setLength(len);
    }
}
```

