inference_trace:
If the string is empty, no steps are needed, so the answer is 0.

If the string is already a palindrome, it can be removed as a single subsequence in one step, so the answer is 1.

Otherwise the answer is 2. All the `'a'` characters together form a palindrome (a string of one repeated letter reads the same both ways), and so do all the `'b'` characters. Removing the `'a'`s in one step and the `'b'`s in another always empties the string.

```java
class Solution {
    public int removePalindromeSub(String s) {
        if (s.isEmpty()) return 0;
        int i = 0, j = s.length() - 1;
        while (i < j) {
            if (s.charAt(i) != s.charAt(j)) return 2;
            i++;
            j--;
        }
        return 1;
    }
}
```

