inference_trace:
Track the robot's position with two counters, `x` and `y`, starting at 0.

- For each character, `'U'` adds 1 to `y`, `'D'` subtracts 1 from `y`, `'R'` adds 1 to `x`, and `'L'` subtracts 1 from `x`.
- Any other character (such as a trailing space in the examples) is ignored.
- After all moves, the robot is back at the origin exactly when both `x` and `y` are 0.

This takes O(n) time and O(1) extra space.

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean judgeCircle(String moves) {
        int x = 0, y = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < moves.length(); i++) {
            char c = moves.charAt(i);
            if (c == 'U') y++;
            else if (c == 'D') y--;
            else if (c == 'R') x++;
            else if (c == 'L') x--;
        }
        return x == 0 && y == 0;
    }
}
```

