inference_trace:
Use BFS/DP over bitmasks of the target's letters. Bit `i` of a mask means target character `i` is already covered.

- `dp[mask]` is the minimum number of stickers needed to reach `mask`.
- Process masks in increasing order. A sticker only adds bits, so transitions always go from a smaller mask to a larger one, and increasing order is valid.
- For each reachable mask and each sticker, apply the sticker greedily:
  - Copy the sticker's letter counts.
  - For each unset bit `i` of the target, if the count for `target[i]` is positive, set bit `i` and decrement that count.
  - Update `dp[newMask] = min(dp[newMask], dp[mask] + 1)`.

Greedy filling is fine here. Positions holding the same letter are interchangeable, so filling any unset positions of a given letter gives an equivalent state for later steps.

**Optimization:** from each mask, only use stickers that contain the first unset character. That character must be covered by some sticker eventually, so this prunes without losing optimality.

**Complexity:** 2^15 masks × 50 stickers × 15 positions ≈ 24M operations, which is fine.

The answer is `dp[full]`, or `-1` if the full mask is unreachable.

```java
class Solution {
    public int minStickers(String[] stickers, String target) {
        int n = target.length();
        int m = stickers.length;
        int[][] cnt = new int[m][26];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (char c : stickers[i].toCharArray()) cnt[i][c - 'a']++;
        }
        int full = (1 << n) - 1;
        int[] dp = new int[1 << n];
        java.util.Arrays.fill(dp, -1);
        dp[0] = 0;
        char[] t = target.toCharArray();
        int[] tmp = new int[26];
        for (int mask = 0; mask < full; mask++) {
            if (dp[mask] < 0) continue;
            int first = -1;
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                if ((mask & (1 << i)) == 0) { first = i; break; }
            }
            int fc = t[first] - 'a';
            for (int s = 0; s < m; s++) {
                if (cnt[s][fc] == 0) continue;
                System.arraycopy(cnt[s], 0, tmp, 0, 26);
                int nm = mask;
                for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                    if ((nm & (1 << i)) == 0 && tmp[t[i] - 'a'] > 0) {
                        tmp[t[i] - 'a']--;
                        nm |= (1 << i);
                    }
                }
                if (dp[nm] < 0 || dp[nm] > dp[mask] + 1) dp[nm] = dp[mask] + 1;
            }
        }
        return dp[full];
    }
}
```

