inference_trace:
A word is uncommon exactly when it appears once in total across both sentences. So I count every word from both sentences in one map, then collect the words whose count is 1.

```java
import java.util.*;

class Solution {
    public String[] uncommonFromSentences(String s1, String s2) {
        Map<String, Integer> count = new HashMap<>();
        for (String w : (s1 + " " + s2).split(" ")) {
            if (w.isEmpty()) continue;
            count.put(w, count.getOrDefault(w, 0) + 1);
        }
        List<String> res = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> e : count.entrySet()) {
            if (e.getValue() == 1) res.add(e.getKey());
        }
        return res.toArray(new String[0]);
    }
}
```

