The constraints are small (`n ≤ 1000`), so a direct simulation is enough: XOR each element `start + 2 * i` for `i` from `0` to `n - 1`.

This runs in O(n) time and uses O(1) extra space.

```java
class Solution {
    public int xorOperation(int n, int start) {
        int res = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            res ^= start + 2 * i;
        }
        return res;
    }
}
```

